[ti:When Speech Recognition Has to Keep Up]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: When I speak to a device, I expect words to appear while I'm still talking.
[00:00.00]Ava：我对着设备说话时，希望还没说完，文字就能显示出来。
[00:05.48]Strong batch accuracy doesn't guarantee that experience.
[00:05.48]批量识别准确率高，并不保证能做到这一点。
[00:09.58]Streaming gives the model only a piece of audio at a time, so both accuracy and response delay can change.
[00:09.58]流式识别每次只给模型一段音频，因此准确率和响应延迟都可能变化。
[00:17.68]Brian: Exactly.
[00:17.68]Brian：没错。
[00:18.43]In a cross-model study cited here, Qwen3-ASR-1.7B had the best batch accuracy among the tested models, yet its WER rose by 77% with 2.4-second chunks.
[00:18.43]这里引用的一项跨模型研究中，Qwen3-ASR-1.7B 的批量识别准确率在受测模型中最高，但使用 2.4 秒音频块时，WER 上升了 77%。
[00:32.46]In that study's streaming comparison, Nemotron Speech Streaming 0.6B had the lowest average WER with 560 ms chunks.
[00:32.46]在该研究的流式识别对比中，使用 560 毫秒音频块的 Nemotron Speech Streaming 0.6B 平均 WER 最低。
[00:43.56]Ava: So the chunk cadence has to be part of the accuracy test.
[00:43.56]Ava：所以，音频块的更新频率也得纳入准确率测试。
[00:47.75]The case study then moves to the newer, multilingual Nemotron 3.5.
[00:47.75]接下来，案例研究转向更新的多语言模型 Nemotron 3.5。
[00:52.61]It asks a practical question: which chunk size and precision give useful transcripts soon enough on an edge device?
[00:52.61]它要回答一个实际问题：在边缘设备上，哪种音频块大小和数值精度能及时产出可用的转写文本？
[01:01.41]Brian: The route starts with ExecuTorch, PyTorch's edge inference framework.
[01:01.41]Brian：这条路线从 PyTorch 的边缘推理框架 ExecuTorch 开始。
[01:06.50]Export prepares the model for inference and produces a .pte file.
[01:06.50]导出过程将模型准备好用于推理，并生成一个 .pte 文件。
[01:11.29]The device runtime loads that file.
[01:11.29]设备端运行时会加载这个文件。
[01:13.88]This gives the authors a way to run the model through a lightweight runtime on the phone.
[01:13.88]这样，作者就能通过轻量级运行时在手机上运行模型。
[01:20.79]Ava: The exported model still needs CPU implementations for its operations.
[01:20.79]Ava：导出的模型仍需要 CPU 实现来执行各项运算。
[01:25.90]How does it reach the optimized Arm routines, and what happens when an operation isn't delegated to XNNPACK?
[01:25.90]它怎样调用经过优化的 Arm 例程？如果某项运算没有委派给 XNNPACK，又会怎样执行？
[01:34.13]Brian: Operations supported for delegation go to XNNPACK.
[01:34.13]Brian：支持委派的运算会交给 XNNPACK。
[01:38.30]On Android, XNNPACK can select KleidiAI microkernels for supported inner matrix calculations.
[01:38.30]在 Android 上，XNNPACK 可以为受支持的内部矩阵计算选择 KleidiAI 微内核。
[01:46.07]Operations not delegated to XNNPACK use ExecuTorch's portable CPU kernels.
[01:46.07]未委派给 XNNPACK 的运算则使用 ExecuTorch 的通用 CPU 内核。
[01:52.25]So export gets the model onto the device, while delegation determines which implementations do the work.
[01:52.25]因此，导出让模型能够在设备上运行，而委派决定由哪些实现来执行运算。
[02:01.28]Ava: And SME2 is one possible acceleration path for matrix work.
[02:01.28]Ava：SME2 也是加速矩阵运算的一条路径。
[02:06.12]But merely enabling it in a build doesn't prove every matrix operation used it.
[02:06.12]但在构建时启用它，并不能证明每项矩阵运算都用到了它。
[02:12.60]We'd need native samples to see which microkernels actually ran.
[02:12.60]我们需要查看原生采样数据，才能知道实际运行了哪些微内核。
[02:18.19]Brian: Right. SME2 extends Arm's instruction set for matrix calculations, including GEMM.
[02:18.19]Brian：对。SME2 扩展了 Arm 的指令集，用于包括 GEMM 在内的矩阵计算。
[02:25.27]In the Arm C1 CPU cluster described here, its matrix unit is shared by cores in that cluster.
[02:25.27]在这里描述的 Arm C1 CPU 集群中，矩阵运算单元由集群内的核心共享。
[02:33.30]KleidiAI provides microkernels that can use the unit for supported operations.
[02:33.30]KleidiAI 提供的微内核可以在受支持的运算中使用这一单元。
[02:40.38]Ava: Let's follow one streaming call.
[02:40.38]Ava：我们来看一次流式调用。
[02:42.79]Nemotron 3.5 uses an RNN-T architecture, so the model has to represent the incoming audio and the tokens it has already emitted.
[02:42.79]Nemotron 3.5 采用 RNN-T 架构，因此模型既要表征传入的音频，也要表征已输出的词元。
[02:52.39]Where are those jobs handled?
[02:52.39]这些工作分别由哪里完成？
[02:54.92]Brian: The encoder represents audio using FastConformer attention and convolution layers.
[02:54.92]Brian：编码器通过 FastConformer 的注意力层和卷积层表征音频。
[03:01.03]The predictor is an LSTM that represents token history.
[03:01.03]预测器是一个表征词元历史的 LSTM。
[03:05.13]Then the joiner combines those representations and predicts a token.
[03:05.13]然后，联合网络结合这两种表征，预测一个词元。
[03:10.20]It can also produce a blank, which moves decoding to the next audio position.
[03:10.20]它也可能输出空白符，让解码移到下一个音频位置。
[03:16.29]Ava: Before the encoder, the frontend makes one log-mel feature vector every 10 ms. The encoder reduces the number of time positions by a factor of 8.
[03:16.29]Ava：进入编码器前，前端每 10 毫秒生成一个对数梅尔特征向量。编码器将时间位置数缩减至八分之一。
[03:27.79]That means each encoder output position represents 80 ms of audio, with fewer positions to decode.
[03:27.79]这意味着编码器的每个输出位置代表 80 毫秒音频，需要解码的位置也更少。
[03:35.91]Brian: At lookahead 13, a call collects 1,120 ms of audio and produces 14 encoder positions.
[03:35.91]Brian：前瞻步数为 13 时，一次调用收集 1,120 毫秒音频，产生 14 个编码器位置。
[03:42.92]The predictor and joiner process all 14 valid positions and add their tokens to the transcript.
[03:42.92]预测器和联合网络处理全部 14 个有效位置，并将输出的词元加入转写文本。
[03:50.75]That amount of audio must arrive before this call can produce its update.
[03:50.75]这段音频必须先全部到达，本次调用才能给出更新。
[03:57.12]Ava: Lookaheads 0, 3, and 6 instead give 80, 320, and 560 ms chunks.
[03:57.12]Ava：前瞻步数为 0、3 和 6 时，音频块分别为 80、320 和 560 毫秒。
[04:02.64]Shorter chunks let the system collect fresh audio more often.
[04:02.64]音频块越短，系统就能越频繁地收集新音频。
[04:07.99]Longer chunks give the model more future context, but the listener waits longer for the first text and later updates.
[04:07.99]音频块越长，模型获得的后续上下文越多，但听众也要等更久才能看到首段文字和后续更新。
[04:18.59]Brian: Preprocessing and inference add time after collection, too.
[04:18.59]Brian：音频收集完成后，预处理和推理也需要时间。
[04:23.10]So the authors measure two different things: transcription quality at each chunk size, and processing time on the device.
[04:23.10]因此，作者分别测量每种音频块大小下的转写质量，以及设备上的处理时间。
[04:32.34]A good WER result alone won't tell us when text appears.
[04:32.34]单凭好的 WER 结果，无法判断文字何时出现。
[04:36.96]Ava: For quality, they run the ExecuTorch runtime with its XNNPACK CPU backend on a host.
[04:36.96]Ava：评估质量时，他们在主机上运行 ExecuTorch，并使用其 XNNPACK CPU 后端。
[04:43.83]A local streaming adapter uses the Open ASR Leaderboard evaluation harness for dataset preparation, transcript normalization, and WER scoring.
[04:43.83]本地流式适配器使用 Open ASR Leaderboard 的评测框架准备数据集、规范化转写文本并计算 WER。
[04:55.43]That's a streaming test rather than a whole-recording batch score.
[04:55.43]这是流式测试，而非对整段录音进行批量识别的评分。
[05:01.17]Brian: Each point covers 14,019 utterances across LibriSpeech Other, AMI Cleaned, Earnings22, and VoxPopuli Cleaned AA.
[05:01.17]Brian：每个数据点涵盖 LibriSpeech Other、AMI Cleaned、Earnings22 和 VoxPopuli Cleaned AA 四个语料库中的 14,019 条语音。
[05:11.77]WER is total word errors divided by total reference words across those four corpora.
[05:11.77]WER 等于这四个语料库的总词错误数除以参考文本的总词数。
[05:19.72]They test FP32, FP16, and INT8 at four chunk sizes.
[05:19.72]他们在四种音频块大小下测试 FP32、FP16 和 INT8。
[05:24.90]Ava: The INT8 choice needs a little care.
[05:24.90]Ava：INT8 的选择需要仔细斟酌。
[05:28.26]Here it's QC8W: eligible linear operations use dynamic INT8 activations and per-channel INT8 weights, with FP32 outputs.
[05:28.26]这里的 QC8W 指：符合条件的线性运算使用动态 INT8 激活值和逐通道 INT8 权重，输出为 FP32。
[05:39.47]So a QC8W run isn't a claim that every operation executes entirely in INT8.
[05:39.47]因此，运行 QC8W 并不意味着所有运算都完全以 INT8 执行。
[05:46.82]Brian: Across these corpora, longer chunks improve final-transcript accuracy.
[05:46.82]Brian：在这些语料上，分块越长，最终转写越准确。
[05:55.46]From 80 to 1,120 ms, FP16 WER falls from 15.2% to 11.5%. QC8W falls from 15.5% to 11.7%.
[05:55.46]分块从 80 毫秒增至 1,120 毫秒时，FP16 的 WER 从 15.2% 降至 11.5%，QC8W 从 15.5% 降至 11.7%。
[06:06.31]That's a meaningful quality change from chunk size alone.
[06:06.31]仅改变分块大小，质量就有明显提升。
[06:13.69]Ava: FP16 differs from FP32 by less than 0.03 percentage points at every chunk size, so the authors leave FP32 out of the later performance analysis.
[06:13.69]Ava：在所有分块大小下，FP16 与 FP32 的差距都不到 0.03 个百分点，因此作者在后续性能分析中省略了 FP32。
[06:28.59]QC8W adds 0.21 to 0.31 percentage points of WER relative to FP32.
[06:28.59]相较 FP32，QC8W 的 WER 高出 0.21 至 0.31 个百分点。
[06:35.32]That makes the precision trade-off fairly specific.
[06:35.32]这样，精度上的取舍就很明确了。
[06:40.95]Brian: But those host scores don't measure when text first appears on the device.
[06:40.95]Brian：但这些主机端分数并未衡量文字何时首次出现在设备上。
[06:46.75]Separately, the authors measure whole-recording processing time on a Google Pixel 11, using a 24.9-second recording and 1,120 ms chunks.
[06:46.75]另外，作者用一段 24.9 秒的录音和 1,120 毫秒的分块，在 Google Pixel 11 上测量整段录音的处理时间。
[06:57.43]One inference thread is pinned to a mid-core CPU, chosen as a representative sustained streaming target.
[06:57.43]一个推理线程固定在 CPU 中核上，以代表持续流式处理的运行条件。
[07:05.94]Ava: They compare two ExecuTorch 1.3.1 builds, with SME2 support switched on or off.
[07:05.94]Ava：他们比较了两个 ExecuTorch 1.3.1 构建版本，分别开启和关闭 SME2 支持。
[07:13.11]Both retain XNNPACK and KleidiAI, and both use identical model artifacts.
[07:13.11]两者都保留 XNNPACK 和 KleidiAI，并使用相同的模型文件。
[07:19.74]Each configuration has two warm-ups and one measured tracing run, so these totals describe that measured run.
[07:19.74]每种配置先预热两次，再进行一次带跟踪的测量，因此这些总耗时描述的是那次测量。
[07:29.98]Brian: With SME2 enabled, FP16 processing falls from 9.79 to 4.61 seconds, a 2.12-times speedup.
[07:29.98]Brian：开启 SME2 后，FP16 的处理时间从 9.79 秒降至 4.61 秒，速度提升 2.12 倍。
[07:40.28]QC8W falls from 5.20 to 3.24 seconds, a 1.61-times speedup.
[07:40.28]QC8W 从 5.20 秒降至 3.24 秒，速度提升 1.61 倍。
[07:47.11]The totals cover the loaded recording from audio preprocessing through final detokenization.
[07:47.11]总耗时涵盖已加载录音从音频预处理到最终解码为文字的全过程。
[07:58.10]Ava: Those processing times are well below the recording's 24.9-second duration.
[07:58.10]Ava：这些处理时间都远低于录音本身的 24.9 秒。
[08:05.51]With SME2 on, the real-time factors are 0.19 for FP16 and 0.13 for QC8W.
[08:05.51]开启 SME2 时，FP16 和 QC8W 的实时因子分别为 0.19 和 0.13。
[08:12.63]That leaves room for other CPU work between chunks, even with one inference thread.
[08:12.63]即使用单个推理线程，分块之间仍有余量处理其他 CPU 工作。
[08:21.18]Brian: There's an important limit to that interpretation.
[08:21.18]Brian：但这一解读有个重要限制。
[08:24.53]Audio still has to arrive before decoding can use it.
[08:24.53]音频必须先到达，解码才能使用。
[08:28.09]Faster processing creates headroom and may help manage thermal load during sustained transcription, but it doesn't erase the wait imposed by the chosen chunk size.
[08:28.09]更快的处理速度增加了余量，也可能有助于控制持续转写时的发热，但无法消除所选分块大小带来的等待。
[08:39.38]Ava: To locate the gain, the authors use ETDump operator timings.
[08:39.38]Ava：为找出性能提升来自哪里，作者使用了 ETDump 的算子耗时数据。
[08:44.23]They group work across the encoder, predictor, and joiner into GEMM, data movement, elementwise work, convolution, normalization, and other operations.
[08:44.23]他们将编码器、预测器和联合网络中的工作分为 GEMM、数据搬运、逐元素运算、卷积、归一化和其他运算。
[08:56.44]Time outside those grouped events appears as residual overhead.
[08:56.44]这些分组事件之外的时间计为剩余开销。
[09:01.89]Brian: GEMM is the main source of the speedup.
[09:01.89]Brian：GEMM 是加速的主要来源。
[09:05.73]For FP16, its summed time drops from 8.2 to 3.1 seconds when SME2 is enabled.
[09:05.73]开启 SME2 后，FP16 的 GEMM 累计耗时从 8.2 秒降至 3.1 秒。
[09:13.31]Its share of total processing time falls from 84% to 67%, though it remains the largest category.
[09:13.31]它在总处理时间中的占比从 84% 降至 67%，但仍是耗时最多的一类。
[09:23.21]Ava: QC8W shows the same shape: GEMM time drops from 4.1 to 2.0 seconds, and its share falls from 78% to 62%.
[09:23.21]Ava：QC8W 呈现相同趋势：GEMM 耗时从 4.1 秒降至 2.0 秒，占比从 78% 降至 62%。
[09:32.89]That explains why speeding up matrix work has a large effect, while also showing that matrix work isn't the whole run.
[09:32.89]这解释了为何加快矩阵运算效果显著，也表明整次运行还有其他耗时。
[09:44.23]Brian: Data movement takes roughly the same time in both builds.
[09:44.23]Brian：两个构建版本的数据搬运耗时大致相同。
[09:49.64]As GEMM gets faster, data movement grows from 8% to 17% of FP16 processing and from 9% to 17% for QC8W.
[09:49.64]随着 GEMM 加快，数据搬运在 FP16 处理时间中的占比从 8% 升至 17%，在 QC8W 中从 9% 升至 17%。
[09:59.44]It's a clearer target for further optimization after the matrix gains.
[09:59.44]矩阵运算加速后，数据搬运成了更明确的后续优化目标。
[10:06.44]Ava: ETDump tells us which operator family costs time, but not which native microkernel executed it.
[10:06.44]Ava：ETDump 能告诉我们哪类算子耗时，却不能指出实际运行的是哪个原生微内核。
[10:13.45]How do we know SME2 code ran on the phone, rather than only being available in the build?
[10:13.45]我们怎么知道 SME2 代码确实在手机上运行，而不只是被编进了程序？
[10:20.37]Brian: Arm Streamline samples native call paths and hardware counters.
[10:20.37]Brian：Arm Streamline 会采样原生调用路径和硬件计数器。
[10:27.43]The sampled GEMM functions confirm SME2-targeted KleidiAI kernels for both FP16 and QC8W on the Pixel 11.
[10:27.43]采样到的 GEMM 函数证实，Pixel 11 上的 FP16 和 QC8W 都运行了面向 SME2 的 KleidiAI 内核。
[10:39.20]The captures also show other paths: some FP16 GEMM uses NEON, and some QC8W GEMM still runs in FP32.
[10:39.20]采样结果也显示了其他路径：部分 FP16 GEMM 使用 NEON，部分 QC8W GEMM 仍以 FP32 运行。
[10:50.75]Ava: Streamline reports 38.4% SME utilization for FP16 and 53.7% for QC8W.
[10:50.75]Ava：Streamline 报告的 SME 使用率，FP16 为 38.4%，QC8W 为 53.7%。
[10:56.70]That measures how much of each capture the matrix hardware was allocated.
[10:56.70]它衡量的是每次采样期间矩阵硬件被分配使用的时间占比。
[11:03.00]It isn't a measure of peak arithmetic throughput, so I wouldn't read those percentages as achieved compute efficiency.
[11:03.00]这不是峰值算术吞吐量指标，因此不能把这些百分比理解为实际计算效率。
[11:13.54]Brian: There's still a tooling gap.
[11:13.54]Brian：工具方面仍有一个缺口。
[11:15.65]ETDump names model operators and their timings; Streamline samples native functions.
[11:15.65]ETDump 给出模型算子名称及耗时；Streamline 则采样原生函数。
[11:21.98]Neither directly maps an individual model layer to the kernel function observed for it.
[11:21.98]两者都无法直接将单个模型层与执行它的内核函数对应起来。
[11:28.54]The authors identify that mapping as future work.
[11:28.54]作者将建立这种对应关系列为未来工作。
[11:32.58]Ava: Now we can choose an operating point.
[11:32.58]Ava：现在可以选择一个运行配置了。
[11:35.40]The article pairs host WER with a Pixel 11 component benchmark.
[11:35.40]文章将主机端 WER 与 Pixel 11 上的组件基准测试结合起来。
[11:40.19]Its first-token number is an estimate: audio collection time plus the median encoder–predictor–joiner sequence time.
[11:40.19]其中的首个 token 时间是估算值：音频采集时间加上编码器、预测器和联合网络序列耗时的中位数。
[11:49.00]It assumes that the first output actually emits text.
[11:49.00]这一估算假定首次输出确实会产生文字。
[11:53.38]Brian: The component benchmark uses synthetic input, fresh stream state, and 75 measured samples per configuration across three rounds.
[11:53.38]Brian：组件基准测试使用合成输入和全新的流状态，每种配置分三轮采集75个测量样本。
[12:09.40]For an illustrative 13% WER ceiling, both precisions qualify at 320, 560, and 1,120 ms. At 320 ms, WER is 12.67% for FP16 and 12.97% for QC8W.
[12:09.40]以13%的WER上限为例，两种精度在320、560和1,120毫秒时均达标。在320毫秒时，FP16的WER为12.67%，QC8W为12.97%。
[12:27.52]Ava: At 1,120 ms, those WERs improve to 11.50% and 11.72%, but audio collection alone takes longer.
[12:27.52]Ava：在1,120毫秒时，两者的WER分别降至11.50%和11.72%，但仅音频采集就需要更长时间。
[12:38.78]If the application has an 800 ms latency budget as well as that 13% WER ceiling, the 320 and 560 ms choices fit both conditions.
[12:38.78]如果应用还有800毫秒的延迟预算，320和560毫秒的选项就能同时满足这两项要求。
[12:54.47]Brian: At 560 ms, FP16 pairs 12.01% WER with an estimated 691 ms delay; QC8W pairs 12.26% with 660 ms. The 80 ms choices miss the illustrated WER target, while the 1,120 ms choices miss the latency budget.
[12:54.47]Brian：在560毫秒时，FP16的WER为12.01%，估计延迟691毫秒；QC8W的WER为12.26%，估计延迟660毫秒。80毫秒的选项达不到示例中的WER目标，1,120毫秒的选项则超出延迟预算。
[13:19.32]It depends on which limits the application must meet.
[13:19.32]具体选择取决于应用必须满足哪些限制。
[13:26.33]Ava: The useful lesson is to test streaming quality at the chunk cadence you'll deploy, then measure device processing separately.
